From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:55:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: stop overriding libhardware_legacy with the
 VNDK v32 prebuilt

The prebuilt copied over /system/lib64/libhardware_legacy.so NEEDs
android.system.suspend@1.0.so, which Android 17 no longer ships; the
source-built library uses android.system.suspend-V1-ndk instead. With
the prebuilt in place every system binary that links libhardware_legacy
fails to link -- vold first ("CANNOT LINK EXECUTABLE ... library
android.system.suspend@1.0.so not found"), and its reboot_on_failure
turns that into a reboot,vold-failed loop before adbd exists. Also hit:
audioserver, dumpstate, libandroid_runtime, libandroid_servers,
libsensorservice, libservices.core-gnss.

The copy was added so the vendor blobs that dlopen the system
libhardware_legacy got the HIDL suspend client they expect. VNDK is gone
in 17 and those blobs (libril-qc-hal-qmi, libcne, libnetmgr, nfc_nci_nxp,
dpmQmiMgr, ...) resolve /vendor/lib64/libhardware_legacy.so, the
source-built copy, so the override has nothing left to serve.

Verified on hardware by replacing the file on the flashed system: boot
proceeds past vold, mount_all, init_user0 and keymaster earlyBootEnded.

---
 msm8996.mk | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/msm8996.mk b/msm8996.mk
index 7f54d01d..0ab6a5ab 100644
--- a/msm8996.mk
+++ b/msm8996.mk
@@ -437,9 +437,6 @@ PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
     vendor/qcom/opensource/vibrator/excluded-input-devices.xml:$(TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR)/etc/excluded-input-devices.xml
 
 # VNDK
-PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
-    prebuilts/vndk/v32/arm64/arch-arm64-armv8-a/shared/vndk-core/libhardware_legacy.so:$(TARGET_COPY_OUT_SYSTEM)/lib64/libhardware_legacy.so
-
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     libcutils-v29 \
     libutils-v33 \
